 "source": "IRAS, HDB",
 "caption": "Fully paid $700K HDB. Keep it and rent it out, or sell and buy a $1.6M condo to rent out? 🏙️\n\nKeep: rent $3,600, keep about $2,300 a month after tax and fees. With 10% growth, up about $208K in 5 years.\n\nSell: $400K down, about $50K stamp duty, rent $5,000. Invest the $230K left at 4% to cover the monthly top up.\nCondo +25%: up about $460K. Condo +10%: about $220K.\n\nBreak even: about 9% growth in 5 years.\n\nComment your flat type and town, and we'll run your numbers 👇\n\nIllustration: 2% loan interest, 25 year loan, 4% return on cash (not guaranteed), 15% tax bracket, 15% deemed rental expenses. Not a forecast.",
